WEBVTT

00:00:02.000 --> 00:00:09.000
<v Rosa Martinez>Okay, let's start. Three things today: the Saguaro compressor, the summer overtime, and the new van.

00:00:10.000 --> 00:00:21.000
<v Rosa Martinez>Saguaro first. Tom Becker emailed again, third visit for the same compressor at the Chandler store, and he's holding the 88011 payment.

00:00:22.000 --> 00:00:36.000
<v Jake Thompson>I looked at the service history. Two different techs, and both replaced the contactor. Nobody checked the refrigerant charge. I think it's low and that's why it keeps tripping.

00:00:37.000 --> 00:00:46.000
<v Rosa Martinez>Then let's send our senior tech. Jake, can you get Luis out there by Wednesday and do a full diagnostic?

00:00:47.000 --> 00:00:50.000
<v Jake Thompson>Yes, Wednesday morning works.

00:00:51.000 --> 00:01:02.000
<v Rosa Martinez>And no trip charge for this visit. I'll call Tom myself today to tell him that and apologize.

00:01:03.000 --> 00:01:15.000
<v Ann Lee>For the record, his invoice 88011 is eighteen seventy-five. Should I hold the reminders on it?

00:01:16.000 --> 00:01:20.000
<v Rosa Martinez>Yes, pause the reminders until it's fixed.

00:01:21.000 --> 00:01:40.000
<v Rosa Martinez>Overtime. We're at about 140 hours a week across the branch. That's not sustainable through August.

00:01:41.000 --> 00:01:55.000
<v Jake Thompson>We could move preventive maintenance visits to early mornings, six to ten, before it gets hot. That frees afternoons for emergency calls.

00:01:56.000 --> 00:02:05.000
<v Rosa Martinez>I like it. Somebody needs to check which customers allow early access.

00:02:06.000 --> 00:02:12.000
<v Ann Lee>I can pull the list of PM customers with access notes.

00:02:13.000 --> 00:02:22.000
<v Rosa Martinez>Great, Ann, by Friday please. Then we decide next Monday.

00:02:23.000 --> 00:02:40.000
<v Jake Thompson>Last thing, the new van. The quote from the dealer expires at the end of the month. Someone should compare it with the lease option.

00:02:41.000 --> 00:02:48.000
<v Rosa Martinez>Let's talk about the van next week. Okay, thanks everyone.
